not a hero is a game from roll seven the  team behind olly olly the incredibly  difficult but fun and challenging  side-scrolling skateboarding game but  not a hero is an action game rather than  a sports game and the story behind it is  a bit ridiculous you as one of I think  about ten characters a lot of which are  unlockable but fighting on behalf of  bunny Lord who is this politician who's  traveled back in time to run for mayor  of the quote-unquote the city and he  wants to win the election so in order to  do that he has got his supporters going  out and fighting crime taking down sort  of the biggest gangsters that are  causing problems for the city  so as you play the game you go through  missions that are filled with various  buildings and one of the biggest and  most important mechanics is cover and  shooting so what you do is you sort of  run enter buildings but you use the a  button to slide from object to object  and your character will automatically  pop and hide behind cover then you then  you know jump out when it's appropriate  to shoot enemies not a hero is a very  fast paced game and by completing  certain challenges that are tied to  performance you unlock stuff so you do  want to play quickly and with a lot of  skill and that can you know depend a lot  on the character you choose some are  slow some are fast some can't use  secondary items but they have really  strong melee attacks some can combine  attack such as sliding and firing at the  same time and all these characters have  pretty funny qualities there's one guy  Jesus or he soos  although the devs call him Jesus he's  loosely modeled after the Jesus from The  Big Lebowski  he's a open shirt wearing guy with a  gold necklace who does a lot of air  thrusting and humping for his idol  animation he's very quick and pretty  funny to play as there's another guy who  is a sort of middle aged man who has  failed at life and now he dons a  superhero masking cape and he's pretty  slow but he says a lot of really funny  things and it's sort of a goal for  people who are trying to play the game  in a different way to test their skill  there are a lot of secondary items to  use in the game that help you strategize  such as grenades and such but grenades  with different behavior and in that  sense it's a little bit like worms when  it comes to the weapon selection things  are absurd but they also have a  strategic element that's very important  to consider not a hero does leave a lot  of room for players who want to be  really good at the game too  practice and come up with their own  strategies and while you can play you  know sort of a stealth heavy game if  you'd like you can also run a gun and  depending on the character you choose  that will make things a little bit more  difficult so trying out the entire cast  familiarizing yourself with their  abilities is pretty important no matter  how you really want to play the game  because ultimately in order to beat it  you're going to have to be good and so  you're gonna have to focus on one style  of play or another at first so not a  hero is coming to PC and early May which  is not too far off and the team recently  updated the build to run at 60 frames  per second and this goes aligned with  this sort of twitch fast paced gameplay  that it's been designed to support so  keep an eye out for not a hero if you  appreciate fast action games and pixel  art style and it will be coming to  PlayStation down the road
 

